1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,180
40!

3
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:35,100
Prodigy?

4
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:36,540
Next time I see you, you're in for it.

5
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:37,950
Leo.

6
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,420
I really believe that with you on the Team,

7
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:41,310
our Jianghai Team winning the Championship is a sure thing.

8
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,300
No doubt about it.

9
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:43,740
And what if I refuse?

10
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,140
The summer Training Camp has been cancelled!

11
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,020
The funding issue for the Jianghai Team,

12
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:49,980
has been completely resolved.

13
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,340
You just don't get it 'cause you're
not the one managing the budget.

14
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:55,740
You little Miser.

15
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,900
Episode 5

16
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,460
Thanks again for the other day.

17
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,860
H-How did you know I was here?

18
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:31,260
Just a coincidence. I was passing by.

19
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,140
They say that meeting by chance more than twice...

20
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,060
means it's no longer just a coincidence.

21
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,460
It means something else.

22
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:46,620
Oh, by the way, I never got your name.

23
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,020
I'm Mini.

24
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,500
Mini?

25
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:52,860
Well, see ya!

26
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,260
Bye!

27
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,020
Leo!

28
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:02,460
Who are you?

29
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:03,660
I'm Mickey!

30
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,900
And this is my Sister, Mini.

31
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,580
Interesting.

32
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:14,940
Hey, don't just smile.
My Sister lent you her Yo-Yo the other day,

33
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,860
and you just walked off like that?

34
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,780
So, what do you want me to do about it?

35
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:22,620
I've got it!

36
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:23,580
Follow me.

37
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:27,900
Don't tell me your big request...

38
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:29,340
is to Challenge me to a Yo-Yo battle?

39
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:32,220
Exactly! And you have to use your Signature Moves.

40
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,100
Fine.

41
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,980
Consider it me returning the favor. Let's go.

42
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,340
Sis, you go first!

43
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,780
Wait, are you on the Jianghai High Yo-Yo Team too?

44
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:20,500
Hmm.

45
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:25,980
My Sister's just a bit off her game today.
Let me take over!

46
00:04:58,020 --> 00:04:59,580
Alright, I'll show you my Secret weapon.

47
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,980
Ferris Flying Saucer!

48
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:14,940
So? Did you see my Saucer?

49
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:18,300
I think I saw it.

50
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,700
Your turn! Remember the deal?

51
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,490
You've gotta use

52
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,000
a move we've never seen before.

53
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,500
Otherwise it doesn't count.

54
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:26,940
Alright.

55
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,500
Fire Warrior!

56
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:53,340
Huh, How can it be this quiet?

57
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,460
So? Did I pass the test?

58
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,740
I'm so stupid. I'm talking to them right now,

59
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,180
but how could they possibly hear me?

60
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,460
What just happened back there?

61
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,820
How come I couldn't hear anything at all?

62
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:33,180
Did you just use a variation of Ferris Flying Saucer?

63
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,620
"Discs Fill the Sky"?

64
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:37,900
That's it! That's really it!

65
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,500
That was "Discs Fill the Sky"!

66
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,500
Mickey, are you okay?

67
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,740
That was incredible!

68
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,140
That move transcends normal speed and sensory perception.

69
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,030
It completely overwhelms your sight and hearing.

70
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,020
They completely stop working.

71
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,420
Exactly. How did you know about that?

72
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:53,790
I read about it in a foreign

73
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,260
professional Yo-Yo magazine.

74
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:57,180
I thought it was just a theory.

75
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,620
I didn't think anyone could actually pull it off.

76
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,060
As long as the theory is correct,

77
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,500
it should be possible.

78
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,390
Not necessarily.

79
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:05,340
At our school, there's this guy named Shawn.

80
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,260
He's always spewing theories.

81
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:10,670
about spatial indexing, light perception, wind speed...

82
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
He makes it sound so complicated.

83
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,980
But when it comes down to it, he can't do any of it.

84
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:14,940
Really?

85
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:18,300
Leo, you've gotta join our School Team!

86
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:19,740
With you on board, the Jianghai Team

87
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,180
will definitely win the Championship!

88
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:25,500
Come on.

89
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:26,940
Let's go to my place. I want to show you something.

90
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:34,110
Wow, so you're the Runner-Up of the

91
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,580
California Chinese Yo-Yo Tournament!

92
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,500
If the Runner-Up is already this incredible...

93
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:39,420
the Champion must be out of this world!

94
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:40,830
Sis!

95
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:43,260
This is a real eye-opener.
There's always someone better out there!

96
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,020
Come on, have some tea! Let's have some tea first.

97
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,380
Thanks, Grandpa.

98
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,380
But we should probably get going.

99
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,780
Come on, Mickey. Let's head out.

100
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,700
If you guys like these magazines,

101
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:57,660
feel free to take them home.

102
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,100
Thanks!

103
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,020
Take your bag with you.

104
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:02,940
Bye! Take care on the road!

105
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:04,860
Take care, you two!

106
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:05,820
Bye, Leo!

107
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:36,060
Grandpa, it's late. You should stop practicing.

108
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,500
Your Sparrowhawk Flip...

109
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:38,940
haven't you already perfected it?

110
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,020
Leo.

111
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:55,230
There's an old Chinese saying:
"Learn. Master. Refine. Perfect. Transcend."

112
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:56,700
I've only reached the "Master" stage with this move.

113
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:00,060
I'm still a long way from the "Transcend" stage.

114
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:02,460
That's why

115
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:05,340
I can't let a single day go by
without practicing with my diabolo.

116
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,620
It's getting late. We should head to bed.

117
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,460
I'm going on ahead.

118
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:25,020
"Learn, Master, Refine, Perfect, Transcend."

119
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:26,940
That's hard to grasp.

120
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,920
But what does that have to do with
the Yo-Yo's Eastern Intuition Style?

121
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,260
I don't see the connection.

122
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,100
But one thing's for sure.

123
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,980
Grandpa doesn't want me to give up practicing.

124
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,300
Hello? Dad?

125
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:57,180
How come your car isn't here yet?

126
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:59,580
No way. He's always so punctual.

127
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,980
Relax, we've still got 5 minutes.

128
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,220
It's here! It's here! Hurry up, Mickey!

129
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:09,180
I know!

130
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:11,580
Dad, the car is here. We're heading out!

131
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:13,980
Be careful out there, okay?

132
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:16,380
We know! We know! Bye, Dad!

133
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:22,620
Our lovely training Camp life is finally about to begin!

134
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,060
Let's go!

135
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,220
Wait! My bag!

136
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,500
Hurry up, Mickey! -Coming, coming!

137
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:02,940
Not bad. From the looks of it,

138
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:05,340
you're on your way to a beauty pageant.

139
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:10,110
Right!

140
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:12,540
And you must be gearing up to
trek solo across the Lop Nur Desert.

141
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:17,820
You two look like you're headed to the World Tennis Cup.

142
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:25,500
Whoa, so cool! Let me think... let me think...

143
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:28,830
I know! You're off to...

144
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:31,260
the annual Las Vegas "King of Gamblers" Tournament! right?

145
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,750
Now, take all that random junk you've got on you,

146
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:43,740
empty it all out and put it on the table.

147
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:44,700
All snacks will be confiscated.

148
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:48,140
Anyone who moves too slow is
out of the Jianghai Team immediately.

149
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,180
Chuck.

150
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:29,340
Listen up, everyone.

151
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,260
We're not here for a vacation.

152
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:32,930
And this isn't a spa retreat.

153
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:34,620
We are here to Train.

154
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:36,540
And what does Training mean?

155
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,380
In the Military, Training means enduring hardship.

156
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,300
Training means discipline.

157
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:43,260
Do you understand?

158
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,870
But we're a Yo-Yo Team, not the army.

159
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:47,580
It's all the same.

160
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,460
Without hardship and discipline,

161
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:51,740
victory is impossible.

162
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:57,180
The purpose of this Training Camp is to forge your willpower,

163
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:00,060
train hard and enhance your Yo-Yo skills.

164
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,940
To overcome all obstacles and strive for the Championship!

165
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:05,340
Alright.

166
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:08,360
Now, take off all those flashy, ridiculous outfits

167
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:10,140
right now!

168
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:11,100
Huh?!

169
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,980
Then... then what are we supposed to wear?

170
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:15,900
Your Team uniforms, of course.

171
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:26,460
Anyone who moves too slow
is out of the Jianghai Team immediately!

172
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:34,620
Not bad. Now you actually look like a real unit.

173
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:41,820
We look like a bunch of beggars.

174
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Shhh!

175
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,940
It doesn't quite fit right.

176
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,820
I'll figure out a better solution later.

177
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:58,140
Everyone just make do for now.

178
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,090
Alright, on my command!

179
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,420
Everyone, attention! Count off!

180
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:07,260
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8!

181
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,210
We only have 7 people. How did we get an "8"?

182
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:19,260
Matthew! One step forward, march!

183
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:28,860
Shawn! What are you doing here?

184
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:30,780
Coach!

185
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:34,620
Yeah! The weather today is just perfect.

186
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:37,020
How about you watch my "Steal the Sky and Swap the Sun" routine?

187
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:40,860
Shawn!

188
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:42,780
How many times have I told you?

189
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:45,180
Making the Team requires going
through the selection process.

190
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:46,150
But your skills...

191
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,390
Maybe next time, okay?

192
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,820
Coach! Coach! Please, just give me one more chance!

193
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,260
Next time, alright? Next time.

194
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:56,500
Coach!

195
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:57,660
Next time! Next time!

196
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:06,300
Count off again!

197
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:11,580
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8!

198
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:15,900
Shawn!

199
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:17,820
Coach Tony!

200
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:20,700
It's Leo!

201
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:25,500
Coach Tony!

202
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:29,860
There's an old saying:
"If fate allows, paths will always cross."

203
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:35,100
Leo! Welcome! Welcome! Come on over!

204
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:37,980
Let me introduce everyone!

205
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:41,310
This is the new member I've made an exception to admit!

206
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,300
Leo!

207
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:48,190
Coach, hold on. That's not really fair, is it?

208
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:51,900
Coach, we all had to pass the tryouts to get here.

209
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,340
What's his deal?

210
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,220
Alright, please don't worry about that, everyone.

211
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:57,660
Me making an exception,

212
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,580
means I have done so for a reason.

213
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,980
Coach Tony, a Student like Shawn,

214
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:03,870
who loves the Yo-Yo with all his heart,

215
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:04,860
couldn't even join the school Team.

216
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:07,740
But you're letting him join so easily?

217
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:10,140
The other Students will be heartbroken.

218
00:18:10,140 --> 00:18:11,500
Alright, that's enough.

219
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:13,500
This decision has already been
approved by the School Administration.

220
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:15,870
And just so you all know,

221
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,340
Leo here

222
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:20,700
is the Runner-Up in the Junior Division

223
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,590
of the California Chinese Yo-Yo Tournament!

224
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,060
Wow, that's awesome!

225
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:25,500
Quiet down.

226
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:30,300
He's just the Runner-Up, you know.

227
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:34,140
Alright! The Jianghai Team members
are all present and accounted for!

228
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,060
Now, our destination...

229
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,500
is Falcon Camp!

230
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:38,460
Move out!

231
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:39,420
Yay!

232
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:48,540
Now what?

233
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:53,340
Hmph. Just you wait.

234
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:16,860
Alright, everyone off!

235
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:18,780
I'm dying of heat!

236
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:21,660
The hardest thing to endure in life
is a van with no A/C!

237
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:26,940
Wow! Am I dreaming?

238
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:30,780
Finally, we're here.

239
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:31,740
Teddy, hurry up!

240
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:32,700
Coming! I'm coming!

241
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:34,140
Nice.

242
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:35,580
Wow, this is amazing!

243
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:40,380
Look! There's a River over there!

244
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:41,820
And there's a Tower, too!

245
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:45,660
Coach! We are more than willing
to endure this kind of hardship!

246
00:19:47,740 --> 00:19:48,540
Go, go, go!

247
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,660
Cost me 2 years of savings...

248
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:01,020
Coach! Come on!

249
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:06,300
Oh, it's beautiful!

250
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:08,700
Matthew, hurry up! Come on!

251
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,540
Which school's summer Camp is this?

252
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,900
I heard it's the Yo-Yo Team from Jianghai High School.

253
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,820
What's a Yo-Yo?

254
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:20,700
It's just a ball tied to a string.

255
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,140
Stop messing with me. How can you even play with that?

256
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:23,100
I've never heard of it.

257
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:25,470
Of course you've never heard of it.

258
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,420
It takes real Skill, you know.

259
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,820
Alright, back to work! Back to work!

260
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:32,220
Back to work!

261
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:35,580
We're here! This is so cool!

262
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,700
Leo! Look, look, look!

263
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,140
See? There's a River over there!

264
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:48,060
And there's a Tower over there, too!

265
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:49,500
Let's go up the Tower!

266
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:51,900
This is awesome!

267
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,260
Look! A huge lotus pond!

268
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:24,060
Leo, what made you suddenly decide to join the School Team?

